  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhanced effectiveness of labour inspection and occupational safety and health systems</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This programme addresses key challenges in labour governance, enterprise competitiveness, and responsible business conduct in Jordan&#x2019;s export-oriented sectors by strengthening national capacity to generate and use evidence on labour markets and working conditions, improving labour inspection and occupational safety and health systems, and supporting enterprises to integrate competitiveness with decent work. It promotes the adoption of responsible business conduct in line with international labour standards and contributes to improved working conditions and access to decent work for workers, including women, migrants, and refugees. Implementation follows a tripartite and multi-stakeholder approach, engaging government institutions responsible for labour and trade, employers&#x2019; and workers&#x2019; organizations, enterprises, and development partners to ensure coordinated, sustainable, and nationally aligned results.</narrative>
  </description>
